module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.discriminating_arm_built_but_never_enrolled

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data discriminating_arm_built_but_never_enrolled: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "discriminating_arm_built_but_never_enrolled" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a claim file builds its discriminating arms and enrols only its accepting control** (the fixtures that would go red are constructed, named and committed, but no assertion consumes them; the one enrolled assertion is the arm whose expected answer is `accepted`, so the file cannot fail on the behaviour it was built to police). ",
    "IT READS AS COVERAGE FROM EVERY ANGLE THAT DOES NOT COUNT ASSERTIONS. The file is named for the property, its receipts are named for the property, the discriminating inputs are present and correct, and a reader tracing the subject finds everything they expect — because everything they expect IS there except the consumption. This is DESIGN section 4b's decoration reached by a different road than a permanently-green check: the check is not weak, it is ABSENT, while the surrounding material asserts it exists. ",
    "THE CHEAP DETECTOR IS A RATIO, NOT A READING: count the constructed fixtures or receipts against the enrolled assertions. `n` receipts and one `test fn` is the signature, and it is decidable without understanding the subject at all. Reading the file for meaning is what FAILS here, because the meaning is entirely correct — the author of the specimen understood the class precisely and wrote the right probes. ",
    "SPECIMEN, and the reason this row does not name a repair: `v2.test.manual.nominal_distinctness_cross_call` constructs three compile receipts — records cross-call, desugared-brands cross-call, and an accepting control — and enrols exactly one `test fn`, `nominal_distinct_control_compiles_ok`. The two discriminating arms have receipts and no assertion. ",
    "THE ARMS CANNOT BE ENROLLED TODAY AND THAT IS THE ACTUAL FINDING. `v2.compiler.00_compile compile_ingest_staging` composes lex, parse, normalize, resolve and translate and NO INFER STAGE, even though `src/v2/compiler/04_infer.dag` exists on disk and is simply not composed into that pipeline. So those receipts cannot form a nominal-mismatch judgment under any keying of any identity: enrolling them as expecting-red would enrol two assertions that are red today and red for as long as staging cannot type. The file is not negligent; it is BLOCKED, and its silence is the only part that is wrong. ",
    "Rung found at 1. CEILING for the enrolment itself is 3 once the capability exists. NEXT TRIGGER, capability and not artifact: a type-judging stage reachable from `compile_ingest_staging`, sufficient for those receipts to yield `Rejected` on a cross-call nominal mismatch — NOT merely the existence of `src/v2/compiler/04_infer.dag`, which already exists and satisfies nothing. Until then the honest state is a declared 4b(2) cannot-climb-until row rather than an unenrolled file that reads as coverage. ",
    "A SECOND SPECIMEN AT A NEW GRAIN, WHICH ALSO SPLITS THIS CLASS IN TWO. The grain above is FIXTURES unconsumed by an assertion; this one is ASSERTIONS unconsumed by the ENTRY. The class is the same and so is the detector once it is stated generally: count DECLARED units against units REACHABLE FROM THE ENTRY, at whatever grain you are standing on. What differs is the blocker. The specimen above is BLOCKED — its arms cannot be enrolled until a capability exists — and that shaped this row's remedy into 'declare the 4b(2) row'. The other half is worse and needs no capability at all: `strategy.workload_benchmark_suite_witness` declared four `test fn`s and left them out of `workload_census_witness_main`'s conjunction. Enrolment was one line. Nothing blocked it, no one declared anything, and the file read as coverage for as long as nobody counted. ",
    "THE HALF WITHOUT A BLOCKER IS THE ONE THAT HIDES A RED. Because enrolment was free, nothing forced a decision, and the unrun claims kept drifting against an authority that moved underneath them: two of the labels one claim asserted that 'no catalog carries' had since been enrolled into the public survey, so the claim was FALSE and had been for as long as it existed. Enrolling the four turned the suite red immediately. A blocked arm at least knows it is not running; a free-to-enrol arm is believed by its author, which is why this half also decays where the blocked half merely waits. ",
    "THE CUT AGAINST `witness_module_absent_from_the_executed_set` IS DISTANCE BETWEEN THE UNIT AND ITS ENTRY, and it is worth stating because the second specimen was nearly filed there. That class is a MODULE not reaching the executed set — the unit and the entry live in different files, so the gap is a composition fact and a reader may reasonably not hold both ends at once. This class is a declaration inside a file whose entry point is a few lines below it: in the second specimen, three. Three lines defeats every reading-based defence simultaneously — not a composition anyone could miss, not a distance anyone could excuse — which is exactly why it needs a mechanical detector rather than more attention. Where the unit and its entry are co-located, absence of consumption is this row; where they are separated by composition, it is the other. ",
    "A CROSS-REPO CLAIM THAT IS NEVER EVALUATED IS INVISIBLE FROM BOTH SIDES, which is why this specimen decayed rather than merely idled. The unrun claim lived in the private repository and asserted a property OF THE PUBLIC SURVEY — that no catalog carried the Blacksmith and WarpBuild labels. The public side then enrolled `blacksmith_label_catalog` and `warpbuild_label_catalog`, which is an ordinary and correct change that no public reviewer could have known falsified a private assertion; and the private side could not notice because nothing evaluated the assertion. Neither repository was negligent and the claim was still false. The general shape: a claim whose subject is an authority in another repository must be EVALUATED to stay true, because no reviewer on either side of the boundary is positioned to catch its decay by reading. ",
    "A THREE-VALUED TYPE DOES NOT MAKE ITS CONSUMERS THREE-VALUED, and this row's second specimen carried that defect beside the enrolment one. `ArmStanding` was split into confirmed / not-confirmed / undetermined precisely so 'the catalog says x64' would stop being confused with 'no catalog knows this label'. The consuming claim then asked `label_is_arm(...) == false`, which is a TWO-VALUED read of a three-valued domain: it is satisfied by both of the arms the split exists to separate, so the fusion reappeared one level up in the consumer while the type below it stayed correct. The tell is mechanical and worth grepping for: `== false` against a predicate over a domain with more than two inhabitants. The repair is a positive reader for the arm actually meant, sourced from the data that arm already carries. ",
    "THE DETECTOR IS STRONGER HERE THAN THE RATIO ABOVE, AND IT IS EXACT. The ratio (constructed fixtures vs enrolled assertions) is a heuristic that needs a reader to judge what counts. For claim files the question is decidable at identity grain: join the declared `test fn` names against the names reachable from the entry point, and the difference is the unrun set — no understanding of the subject required, no count to calibrate. Two cautions learned running it: the join must follow helper conjunctions (`all_scan_claims_hold`) and not just the entry's own body, or it reports false positives; and the failure REPORT must cover the same set as the conjunction, since a report listing a prefix of the claims makes the resulting red anonymous. ",
    "THE CONTROL THAT SEPARATES THE TWO HALVES IS ONE MUTATION. Mutate the claim so it must go red, and run the ENTRY POINT rather than the claim. If the entry still exits 0, the claim is not enrolled — which is how this specimen was found, after its positive control had already exited 0 and established nothing. DESIGN section 5 names the general rule ('a typecheck and a grep are not consumers'); this is the operational form: a green entry point is evidence only once a mutation has made it red. ",
    "SUBJECT BOUNDARY ON THE FIRST SPECIMEN, recorded because these two were conflated once already during this row's own discovery. It bounds that specimen and NOT this class, which the second specimen shows is indifferent to subject and to repository: the FIRST specimen is about v2 RECORD nominal distinctness through the staging pipeline — `type IntentId { value: String }`, which is what a brand looks like AFTER desugaring. It is NOT the `where brand(\"...\")` refinement walled in gunbc#10337, which is a v1 `04_infer` concern. Same word, two representations, two pipelines; a reader who merges them will conclude the wall already covers this and it does not. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
